      "notes": [
        "Printed: plan identifies apartment 4, total 89.4 m2; table also totals 89.4 m2. Room numbers 1 through 8 map to hall, living, kitchen, bed4, bed5, bath6, bath7, balcony.",
        "Measured: scale 57.25 pixels/metre, checked against bedroom 5 width 174px / 3.05m, bedroom 4 width 155px / 2.70m, living width 200px / 3.50m, and bedroom 5 height 235px / 4.10m. Origin is plan pixel [477,345].",
        "Measured: polygons trace inside faces; grey and hatched bands define walls. Hall opens into living below the short kitchen partition. Kitchen opens south into living. No wall follows the cyan dimension lines.",
        "Derived: the hall includes its lower circulation arm; the printed 5.15 by 2.15 dimensions describe only its upper portion. The living 8.20 dimension is printed along its long extent. Areas are copied from the table, not calculated from polygons.",
        "Assumed: no photos were supplied. All floor and wall colours, 2.8m ceiling height, door heights, window sill 0.35m and head 2.60m are provisional, not observed finishes.",
        "Measured: entrance is the gap in the north facade; balcony has separate doors from bedroom 4 and living, plus bedroom glazing. All opening widths span their drawn gaps.",
        "Derived: crossed narrow grey strips at bathroom west sides and kitchen north are service shafts represented as solid wall thickness, not habitable floor. Cyan crossed balcony object is interpreted as an outdoor utility unit.",
        "Assumed: kitchen wall cabinets and oven below the drawn hob are inferred; fixtures and fitted wardrobes otherwise follow plan symbols. Bathroom 7 is interpreted as an open shower area with the shower fitting drawn at its lower left; no bath is drawn. No unshown radiators or washing machine added.",
        "Assumed: balcony exposed west and south edges have 1.10m railings; no full-height walls are invented there.",
        "Measured: inside-face traced areas differ from the printed schedule, most noticeably hall 17.08 versus 18.4 m2. Printed values are preserved; geometry follows the drawn wall faces rather than enlarging rooms to force agreement."
